/-! # The run of class 666 (R = 23): `E1Concl Em 23` and its row (generated by a script)

The run is the list `BLK.lits` of 101 pieces (by a script: the trace block split into a mode-0 root and
mode-1 / restart pieces), checked in `B0` … `B5` (`blkChk`) and glued by the witness table `W` (`glueChk`). It is replayed here
against the IP's own slot function `sl` (slots from the row-table entries). With `ipok` and `rows`, `E1GS.e1_sound`
gives `E1Concl Em 23`; `rowValid_of_e1` (padding, `oneOK`, `emOK`) then gives the class's row at `lbOf 666 = 24`.
`run_666 : Tab2.HighHyp 666 → RowValid (Tab2.basisOf 666) (Tab2.lbOf 666)` is the form `Tab2/Dispatch.lean` takes. -/

